  "usage_note": "Use **on** before a day: *on Friday*. *On Fridays* means every Friday. There is no preposition before **next**, **last**, **this**, or **every**: *next Friday*. In American English, **on** is often left out in speech: *See you Friday*. The short written form is **Fri.**",
